    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1463">

                <pb facs="1235" n="1131" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg1131"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.55/34.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-11-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 14, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Panaman Government has at last moment withdrawn clause conveying ultimatum and
                    reopened negotiations. No arrests made and period of ten days granted to allow
                    further consideration by the Chinese of Government’s altered requirements with
                    regard to application of Law 50. Panaman Government offers upon registration the
                    issuance of a new and more satisfactory cédula confirming acquired rights of
                    Chinese.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wicker</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
